Use the core urlEncode() BIF instead of encodeForURL() in Portcullis

Masa's Portcullis.removeNullChars() calls encodeForURL(), which Lucee only
provides through the ESAPI extension. Our images ship a minimal extension set
(see the `extensions` argument of mkLuceeDockerImage), so the function is
undefined at runtime and every request that passes through Portcullis - i.e.
all of them - blows up. urlEncode() is a core BIF and does the same job here,
since the result is immediately urldecode()d again after stripping %00.

Upstream commit this was extracted from:
emotions-ch/praxisgemeinschaft-zuerichhorn.ch@fbfe177

--- a/core/mura/Portcullis.cfc
+++ b/core/mura/Portcullis.cfc
@@ -618,7 +618,7 @@

 	<cffunction name="removeNullChars" access="private" output="false">
 		<cfargument name="theString" type="string" required="true" />
-		<cfreturn urldecode(replace(encodeForURL(arguments.theString),"%00","","all"))>
+		<cfreturn urldecode(replace(urlEncode(arguments.theString),"%00","","all"))>
 	</cffunction>

 </cfcomponent>
